  (text "1. LED current = 0.1 V / R_SENSE (R5, R11): 0.068R is about 1.5 A. Set to the emitter's rating and verify the AL8860 sense voltage."
    (at 20.32 176.97 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 3e2a1608-07a2-56db-8837-fac19ae4fbc3)
  )
  (text "2. CTRL network: R3/R9 4.7k from the PWM input, R4/R10 100k to GND, NTC (10k B3950) from CTRL to GND at the emitter. Hot NTC pulls CTRL down and reduces current."
    (at 20.32 180.78 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid cfb36050-702d-53f9-8823-7f5ddd816a98)
  )
  (text "3. Check the AL8860 CTRL voltage range and internal pull-up, then adjust R3/R4 (R9/R10)."
    (at 20.32 184.59 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid caabe42f-6622-5e86-91e6-475cfa2c8b44)
  )
  (text "4. C2/C6 (DNP) turn high-frequency PWM into smooth analog dimming when fitted."
    (at 20.32 188.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 1f5fe980-f145-51cc-bc3c-9dbc0834acd7)
  )
  (text "5. On 4S packs the LED string's forward voltage must stay below about 11 V."
